        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>base</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="group__cputimer__api_1ga214aff735b0acf172ffe29ebe591fe61" kindref="member">CPUTimer_ClockSource</ref></type>
          <declname>source</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="group__cputimer__api_1gafa70b7d5a2a5b33b6bd56e84ff1cec4d" kindref="member">CPUTimer_Prescaler</ref></type>
          <declname>prescaler</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Select CPU Timer 2 Clock Source and Prescaler</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>base</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the base address of the timer module. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>source</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the clock source to use for CPU Timer 2 </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>prescaler</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is the value that configures the selected clock source relative to the system clock</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
This function selects the specified clock source and prescaler value for the CPU timer (CPU timer 2 only).</para>
<para>The <emphasis>source</emphasis> parameter can be any one of the following:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_SOURCE_SYS</bold> - System Clock</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_SOURCE_WROSCDIV8</bold> - WROSC (Wide Range Oscillator) output clock after the fixed BY8 divider</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_SOURCE_SYSOSCDIV4</bold> - SYSOSC output clock after the fixed BY4 divider</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_SOURCE_XTAL</bold> - External Clock</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The <emphasis>prescaler</emphasis> parameter can be any one of the following:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_PRESCALER_1</bold> - Prescaler value of / 1</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_PRESCALER_2</bold> - Prescaler value of / 2</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_PRESCALER_4</bold> - Prescaler value of / 4</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_PRESCALER_8</bold> - Prescaler value of / 8</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CPUTIMER_CLOCK_PRESCALER_16</bold> - Prescaler value of / 16</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>None. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
